		{"id":"b49f16cc02bb0f07","type":"link","url":"https://perso.telecom-paristech.fr/boubek/papers/DAG_Amendment/","x":-11971,"y":-1590,"width":1051,"height":796},
		{"id":"9554cc3bbb09de8c","type":"text","text":"* Parametric model offers number of parameters\n* Generation step: final model is generated once parameters are set","x":-11720,"y":-1760,"width":549,"height":106},
		{"id":"ea88091abee1da69","type":"text","text":"Procedural modeling = algorithmical modeling","x":-11802,"y":-2142,"width":631,"height":60},
		{"id":"71087710fde7c92f","type":"text","text":"# What is procedural modeling?","x":-11772,"y":-2282,"width":572,"height":66},
		{"id":"0b7b4fed8e9335d0","type":"text","text":"Procedural modeling is modeling approach where model (geometry, texture, story, terrain, etc.) is described by a set of rules and algorithms applied on certain data (e.g., geometry).\n\nRules are either written in certain programming language (e.g., c++, python, VEX, OSL, GLSL, etc.) or using node based system (visual programming).\n\nResulting model is completely described by a set of rules. Each of rule can be changed completely or by parameters resulting in different version of a model.\n\nMany advantages come out of this approach as we will see. However, it is not a silver bullet!","x":-12519,"y":-774,"width":631,"height":332},
		{"id":"346db52a3351db37","type":"text","text":"Algorithm: authoring step\n> A process or set of rules to be followed in calculations or other problem-solving operations, especially by a computer.","x":-12520,"y":-1871,"width":488,"height":140},
		{"id":"28961332a9600b4b","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/ProcParadigms/Algorithm.jpg","x":-12519,"y":-1692,"width":487,"height":387},
